// The livingbody package: bodies that look alive. A program reaches it with 'import livingbody'.
//
// A body that is only posed looks like a statue even when the pose is a good one. What is added here is the small,
// continual motion that keeps a standing person alive, in the four kinds that the animation of the best-made games
// carries: breathing, idle motion, secondary motion and looking.
//
//   breath.cone     ONE breathing clock: its rate and depth set by exertion (rest, a walk, a run, and the panting that
//                   follows it, which settles back over time), a lung-fill waveform with inspiration, expiration and
//                   pause, and the body's shape and bones in it; the FaceRig breathes the same fill (setBreath)
//   idle.cone       the weight shifting from foot to foot, a table of fidget gestures, and attention: what to look at
//                   next and for how long (the face rig then moves the eyes and head; the look-at chain the neck)
//   soft.cone       soft regions: morph targets (built by facerig's own soft-selection machinery) that breathe and a
//                   damped spring per region that lags and rings, on top of skinning: a belly, a chest, a cheek, a flank
//   humanoid.cone   LivingHumanoid: all of it composed over a base pose by animlayers for the 19-bone figure
//
// Layering is animlayers' (additive and override layers with bone masks, limb pins, a look-at chain); hair, manes, tails and
// anything else that is a strand in a flow are strandflow's.
//
// WHAT IS NOT HERE, on purpose: a balance or posture system (a creature's weight over its feet in every posture:
// Backlog\creature-animation.md); avatar customisation; any particular character.
//
// Conventions are bonepose's: right-handed, y up, metres, f32; a being faces -z; its left is -x.

mod livingbody;

import libc;
import collections use *;
import geomath use *;
import mesh use Mesh;
import bonepose use *;
import poseik use *;
import facerig use *;
import animlayers use *;
